      "message": "I think it used to be common to name tests this way but in the recent years it\u0027s actually more recommended to name the tests as a statement/fact that summarizes the expected behavior[1][2].\n\nIn addition, for Java or Rust, we don\u0027t need \"test\" in test name as the annotation already indicates it\u0027s a test (for some other languages like Python it was mandatary to name a test with \"test\" otherwise the test runner cannot recognize it). The current name also contains one more piece of information that it\u0027s the protected VM that runs pvmfw.\n\n[1] https://enterprisecraftsmanship.com/posts/you-naming-tests-wrong/\n[2] http://go/unit-testing-practices#naming",
