      "writtenOn": "2022-12-05T20:58:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Well, we can move this log to the beginning of [1] to be more sure for now.\n\nNo, we can\u0027t as this would hang the VM.\n\n\u003e Considering that this feature is for Android U\n\n`DeathReason` from post-pvmfw stages (bootloader (now gone), init, ...) is already supported and VS should return `DeathReason::Shutdown` if the VM issues a PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF.\n\nIn turn, this test could expect the shutdown by using the simplest init possible that turns off the VM (an even better approach would be to have a dedicated \"kernel\" that simply PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF but not sure how to integrate that into the testing infra).\n\n\u003e Not sure how to check that DeathReason::Shutdown according to the existing examples ...\n\nMe neither; @shikhapanwar@google.com, any idea?\n\n\u003e ... and how stable that can be.\n\nWhy wouldn\u0027t it be stable? We are checking that the VM performed a clean shutdown.",
      "parentUuid": "e7acc4cf_28a8ebd9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 436,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 436,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "c2f9517a853f08931f5244c2ae527989e5fd5629",
