      "writtenOn": "2022-12-05T21:30:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why the VM should issue a PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF after successfully booting pvmfw?\n\n\u003e Why wouldn\u0027t it be stable? \n\nI agree the idea is clean. I mean taking a new approach at this stage can have a high maintenance cost (like we might need to spend lots of time to address the flakiness like [1]), I don\u0027t mean the approach itself, but the intermediate functions we\u0027ll use to connect different pieces together.\n\nBy nature e2e tests have better coverage in comparison with unit test because they test longer flows, but the trade-off is that they are slow, flaky and are often harder to maintain.\n\n[1] the recent automatically reported flakiness of this class http://b/issues?q\u003dMicrodroidHostTestCases%20reporter:android-growler",
      "parentUuid": "83e3d71a_c1b392ac",
